answer 2: Why it matters to someone who does not follow this subject: This is the official monthly count of jobs and unemployment, arriving after the Federal Reserve's quarter-point increase on September 16, with August PCE inflation at 3.4 percent and average hourly earnings up 3.0 percent over the year. (`bls-empsit-2026-09`; `fomc-statement-2026-09-16`; `bea-pce-2026-08`)
  /Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/src/pages/events/jobs/2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000.astro:62: The Federal Reserve's two goals are maximum employment and price stability. On September 16 the Federal Open Market Committee raised the target range for the federal funds rate by 1/4 percentage point. The committee's goals statement says it &ldquo;considers a wide range of indicators&rdquo; in assessing maximum employment. This report's small payroll gain and little-changed unemployment are evidence the committee will weigh on October 27-28, and the October decision is not known. The next employment report, for October, is scheduled for November 6. On prices, the personal consumption expenditures price index for August, whose annual change is how the committee measures inflation, was up {admitted.pceAugust} percent from a year earlier. This report put average hourly earnings up 3.0 percent over the past 12 months.
  /Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/src/pages/events/jobs/2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000.astro:63: Chris Phelan, chair of the President's Council of Economic Advisers, argued that the central bank's decision to raise rates last month was a mistake because inflation is already coming down. The Federal Open Market Committee's September 16 statement says &ldquo;Inflation remains elevated.&rdquo; Philip N. Jefferson, a vice chair of the Federal Reserve Board, said on October 1 that he supported that decision because he saw it as the appropriate policy to pursue the Fed's dual mandate. He also said he sees &ldquo;economic activity and labor market conditions remaining broadly solid while inflation remains above our target.&rdquo;
  /Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/src/pages/events/jobs/2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000.astro:64: Reuters wrote that the slowdown was &ldquo;almost taking another interest rate hike from the Federal Reserve this month off the table&rdquo;. The same dispatch said financial markets initially lowered bets on a rate hike at the October 27-28 meeting to {yardsticks.hikeOddsLow} percent before lifting them to about {yardsticks.hikeOddsLater} percent, little changed from Thursday, CME Group's FedWatch tool showed.
