answer 4: The one concept a stranger must hold to follow it, the mechanism: The 29,000 and the 4.2 percent rate come from two different surveys, one a net change in jobs on employer payrolls and the other a count of people. (`bls-empsit-2026-09`)
  /Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/src/pages/events/jobs/2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000.astro:61: The establishment survey counts jobs on employer payrolls, and the household survey counts people. The payroll figure comes from the first and the unemployment rate from the second, so the two can move differently in one month.
